WEBVTT

00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:03,740
All right, welcome everybody to today's Zoom call.

00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:08,540
Today we're gonna talk about some promising cancer solutions

00:00:08,540 --> 00:00:11,940
that are on the rise.

00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:15,700
Patient asked me about this, so I wanted to address it.

00:00:15,700 --> 00:00:20,340
One is this new CAR-T cell therapy,

00:00:20,340 --> 00:00:22,740
and so that's what we're gonna talk about first.

00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:27,740
CAR-T cell therapy is where they remove your T cells,

00:00:28,580 --> 00:00:30,780
they remove your blood, separate out the T cells,

00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:34,620
so T cells are part of your immune system killer cells,

00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:37,340
and then they adapt the T cells

00:00:37,340 --> 00:00:40,620
similar to what is done with the immunotherapy

00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:43,660
that is out there like Kutruda,

00:00:43,660 --> 00:00:46,380
but they're actually adapting your own T cells

00:00:46,380 --> 00:00:49,340
and changing the receptor sites on your own T cells

00:00:49,340 --> 00:00:52,820
so that they'll be attracted to that cancer.

00:00:52,820 --> 00:00:55,300
So it's a really exciting therapy

00:00:55,300 --> 00:01:00,300
and I'm gonna try to share my desktop here

00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:05,620
so that I can show you this video of CAR-T cell therapy

00:01:09,900 --> 00:01:14,380
from MD Anderson.

00:01:14,380 --> 00:01:18,420
So hopefully this will work, so you can listen to this.

00:01:18,420 --> 00:01:23,100
This is the immune system that's helped to fight off infections.

00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:27,100
T cells can react and kill cancer cells

00:01:27,100 --> 00:01:28,660
in the right circumstances.

00:01:28,660 --> 00:01:32,420
The problem is that some of the cancers can evade

00:01:32,420 --> 00:01:34,180
the immune system.

00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:36,780
CAR-T cell therapy is very unique in different

00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:38,580
than any other treatment that we've had.

00:01:38,580 --> 00:01:42,980
It's a treatment where we take the patient's own T cells

00:01:42,980 --> 00:01:45,300
and we modify them in a laboratory

00:01:45,300 --> 00:01:49,860
so that they can recognize and react against their cancer.

00:01:49,860 --> 00:01:51,580
The patient undergoes a ferrisis,

00:01:51,580 --> 00:01:53,860
which is the process of removing the T cells.

00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:57,580
We modify them in a laboratory to express receptors

00:01:57,580 --> 00:01:59,340
to better recognize cancer.

00:01:59,340 --> 00:02:03,180
Those T cells are then expanded and grown to large numbers

00:02:03,180 --> 00:02:06,420
and we re-infuse those modified T cells

00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:08,860
back into the patients through an IV.

00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,940
The CAR-T cells that are generated

00:02:12,940 --> 00:02:15,300
all have a similar receptor on them

00:02:15,300 --> 00:02:18,860
and this receptor recognizes a cancer cell.

00:02:18,900 --> 00:02:21,700
Patients can get flu-like symptoms

00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:24,700
or neurologic symptoms from the treatment.

00:02:24,700 --> 00:02:26,580
Right now, we're giving patients

00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,300
partisotherapy in the hospital

00:02:28,300 --> 00:02:30,940
because their symptoms can become very severe.

00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:34,940
We're currently treating childhood and young adults

00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:36,820
acute lymphoblastic leukemia.

00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:38,580
In addition, we're treating patients

00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:40,620
with non-hatch canzum phoma,

00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:43,740
particularly diffuse large b-cellum phoma.

00:02:43,740 --> 00:02:46,100
MD Anderson researchers are working

00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:48,540
to expand application of heart T cells

00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:54,500
to other cancers, including solid tumors.

00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:59,500
So that is some excited therapy that is on the way,

00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:05,260
we hope, and the problem is right now

00:03:05,260 --> 00:03:08,820
it's really only been FDA approved

00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:11,340
for some childhood leukemias

00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:14,220
and certain types of lymphoma.

00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:16,100
So it's not available for everyone.

00:03:17,340 --> 00:03:18,660
And there's other problems to it.

00:03:18,660 --> 00:03:19,980
I wanna address that too.

00:03:19,980 --> 00:03:23,500
I was actually gonna do a video on this a few weeks ago

00:03:24,500 --> 00:03:27,980
and do a post on this.

00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:29,580
So I really get this on Facebook

00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:30,860
but then somebody asked the question,

00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:32,660
so I thought I'd better do this.

00:03:32,660 --> 00:03:35,860
So really what's done with heart T therapy

00:03:35,860 --> 00:03:38,180
is that you're collecting the person's own blood,

00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:39,820
they're taking the T cells,

00:03:39,820 --> 00:03:43,980
they're changing the receptor site on the T cell.

00:03:43,980 --> 00:03:47,140
Because remember, one of the problems with fighting cancer

00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:50,820
is that cancer cells are your own body cells.

00:03:50,820 --> 00:03:53,460
They're not a virus or bacteria

00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:56,580
that is an enemy trying to kill your body.

00:03:56,580 --> 00:03:58,540
So your immune system isn't supposed

00:03:58,540 --> 00:04:00,340
to react to your own cells.

00:04:00,340 --> 00:04:02,140
That's what if you don't therapy does too,

00:04:02,140 --> 00:04:07,140
is it changes that receptor site on the T cells

00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:08,980
as they attack the cancer,

00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:11,060
but it's done through a drug.

00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:14,300
Heart T therapy is taking out your blood,

00:04:14,300 --> 00:04:17,460
changing your T cells, reproducing them in the laboratory,

00:04:17,460 --> 00:04:18,700
putting them back in the body

00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:20,860
so that they start fighting the body.

00:04:20,860 --> 00:04:21,980
Start fighting the cancer.

00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:25,940
The problem is is that it will start fighting all cells

00:04:25,940 --> 00:04:29,780
and that's what the doctor was alluding to that short video.

00:04:30,820 --> 00:04:33,580
And you can get even a worse autoimmune reaction

00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:35,740
that you can with a ketruda.

00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:40,060
But you can get a good kill of the cancer.

00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:42,620
So there's some promising to it.

00:04:43,340 --> 00:04:47,180
Problem that they're having with it is the cost.

00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:51,860
So an article that I was going to share a few weeks ago

00:04:51,860 --> 00:04:54,020
